    <string name="guide_1_desc">Tap ＋ Add script and pick one: Browse files (from device folders), Import from link (download .sh), or Manual input (absolute path).</string>
    <string name="guide_1_title">① Add scripts</string>
    <string name="guide_2_desc">Tap Run in order to execute scripts one by one. When a script asks something, the orange prompt row shows the question — type your answer below. Color terminal plus automatic GBK/UTF-8 detection are supported.</string>
    <string name="guide_2_title">② Run &amp; interact</string>
    <string name="guide_3_desc">Answers from manual runs are recorded automatically. Go to Presets to save the whole queue — one tap replays it with answers auto-filled, and can jump to a target app when done.</string>
    <string name="guide_3_title">③ Record &amp; replay</string>
    <string name="guide_4_desc">Queue row dots: green = success, red = failed (non-zero exit code), orange = running (edge bar), grey = pending. Failed scripts show their exit code.</string>
    <string name="guide_4_title">④ Status colors</string>
    <string name="guide_5_desc">Browse any folder (via root), quick chips jump between favorites; the ⋯ menu offers details, edit, permissions, rename and delete; tapping a script adds it to the queue.</string>
    <string name="guide_5_title">⑤ Files tab</string>
    <string name="guide_6_desc">Top-right 中/EN switches language; ☾ toggles day/night theme; tap the Queue title to collapse the list and give the terminal more room; Stop aborts the whole queue.</string>
    <string name="guide_6_title">⑥ Tips</string>
    <string name="guide_7_desc">Execute does nothing → check the Root status row and whether the queue is empty; script failed → red [script exit code: n] in the terminal, scroll up for errors; change a recorded answer → run manually again and type the new answer, it overwrites; garbled Chinese → the terminal auto-switches UTF-8/GBK, no action needed.</string>
    <string name="guide_7_title">⑦ FAQ</string>
